Hi all!

Wow, after playing Nethack for like ever, I've finally ascended my first
character!

Thanks again to the kind souls on r.g.r.n who replied to my post in
January asking for help. I have since been playing the same savegame very
slowly and have ascended that same savegame :)

It was not supposed to be like this. I was /supposed/ to by using my
fileserver to play all of my Nethack games, so that I could have a
centralised high-score file, but one 'quick' game on my work laptop
spiraled into an ascension after many fortunate events (and a few months
delay because of real-life stuff!)

An early WoW provided nice armour and goodies early on which really
helped. I died twice falling into pits while wielding cockatrice corpses,
luckily I was wearing an amulet of life saving each time - following the
advice given to my earlier post - Thanks!

Killed Asmodeus on dlvl:33, Vlad in his tower at dlvl:35, Orcus and
Yeenoghu on dlvl:41. Spent ages trying to figure out how to get into the
center of the level dlvl:43-46 but eventually figured it out a bit lower
down.  Rodney was there in the tower and kept double-troubling, causing me
lots of problems until he foolishly summoned a cockatrice which I used to
mash everything in the tower. (Bwhahahahahaha). A very welcome moment of
relief in what was a very very scary situation. (First meeting with
Rodney, surrounded by lots of him and other monsters!)

Got the book, headed down and then flailed around trying to do the
invocation at the VS on dlvl:50 for quite a while, summoning nasties each
time I got it wrong, until eventually I got it right and opened the stairs.

Had to do a hard slog through the level to get the amulet on dlvl:51.
Rodney showed up some more but was dealt with by my wand of death.  Then
run!  On the way up I was dragged back a few levels about 6 times but it
wasn't a problem really.  Rodney kept showing up but my wands held out to
the end of the game - phew!

Gradually my stuff was getting cursed and I had run out of potions of
holy-water.  It was with great nervousness when I left the dungeon at
dlvl:1 for the first time - fortunately the next few levels of planes
didn't cause my character a problem at all. The plain of water is weird
though, it was tricky bouncing around in the bubble of air. Next time, I'm
going to be a bit braver and will try using an amulet of magical
breathing to see if I can move about outside the bubble.

Astral was scary. Right at the start someone whispered to me and gave me
an angel pet which was really tough and lasted most of the level helping
me out.  I knew it was the last level from what I'd heard on #nethack.
This level took me about 2 hours to do. I chose the wrong altar each time
and only found Odin's altar last after a very hard slog. My max hp had
been reduced from 360+ by some (or one) of the riders, not sure which as
it all became a bit of a blur!

After spying Odin's altar I did not hesitate and offered it immediately,
sinking back into my chair as the choir sang. I am the happiest and most
pleased man alive. Thank you Nethack dev-team, Thank you to r.g.r.n and
Thank you #nethack.  I think I need to sleep for 5 months though! *off to
buy chocolate ice-cream as a reward now :)*

Johnny
(aka IcyValk77)



